  "hostNotes": "Accept any town or gazetted locality the road actually passes through between Torquay and Allansford (plus Warrnambool), and be generous with near-misses a few km up a side road (Johanna, Cape Otway, Timboon, Deans Marsh); Geelong, Colac, Winchelsea, the Bellarine towns, Port Fairy and Portland are not on the road and can be rejected - decide before the round and apply it consistently. Landmarks are not towns: Twelve Apostles (ask for the town - Princetown), Loch Ard Gorge, London Bridge, Cape Patton, Memorial Arch, Erskine Falls, Otway Fly and 'the Otways' should be bounced or redirected, with Bells Beach the one exception because it is also a locality. Merge spelling variants (Aireys/Airies/Airys, Anglsea, Port Cambell, Kennet, Skeens) and remember Separation Creek is where the house is, so expect it to be said by several people rather than scoring as rare."
